<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jorhat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jorhat is a city in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/upper-assam">Upper Assam</a>, north-east <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, near the south bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmaputra">Brahmaputra</a> and the headquarters of Jorhat district. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaurinath-singha">Gaurinath Singha</a> moved the Ahom capital there in 1794, and it remained the seat of the last Ahom kings until the Burmese invasions. Today it is a centre of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tea">tea</a> industry, home to the Tocklai tea research station and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> Agricultural University.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jorhat.jpg" alt="Jorhat" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Arb assam · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Tarun_Ram_Phukan_Road_Jorhat.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
